      "side": 1,
      "message": "As I mentioned to you offline, I think this will create a ref-cyle in:\n\nPipeline -refs-\u003e PipelineLayout -refs-\u003e BindGroupLayout -refs-\u003e Pipeline.\n\nWe will need to somehow break this cycle if we want to keep this as is, otherwise I believe that this will cause a potential memory leak of these objects.\n\nSeparately though, after reviewing the change and talking with Shrek to understand this a bit more, I actually think it might make more sense to save something like a `std::pair\u003cRef\u003cPipeline\u003e, BindGroupIndex\u003e` in the `webgpu::BindGroup` instead when it is created with an implicit `BindGroupLayout`. If we do that, then I\u0027m pretty sure we avoid the ref cycle entirely, and IIUC, the only time we even need to recreate the pipeline to get the `BindGroupLayout` from it is when we want to create a `BindGroup` using the specific layout. This also has the added benefit of keeping this detail in the webgpu backend instead of having to push it up to the frontend.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 80,
        "endChar": 49
      },
      "revId": "bd9b48b3f6e64262f8fe233a235d8ea50ecb9463",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
